  "upstream_tests_run": false,
  "findings": [
    "Whole README/license/Vite config/package/gitignore/Blender note/Draco README and five shader files read. Room portfolio rendering, audio and theme animation; these files implement no duplicate search. Package scripts offer dev/build/preview, no test script. No dependency installation, server launch or upstream instructions executed.",
    "Root MIT notice and bundled Draco README Apache2 notice are distinct. Third-party asset credits/commercial-license assertion in README do not establish blanket asset relicensing. GLSL samples animate smoke and blend day/night textures; no perceptual hash, image similarity or exact comparison here. Domain rejection supported for reviewed files only;111 blobs remain unassessed in full.",
    "Whole2114line src/main.js read in contiguous ranges1..380,381..1000,1001..1600,1601..EOF. Entire entrypoint implements Howler audio, Three scene/camera, GLTF/Draco model loading, baked day/night textures, smoke/video materials, GSAP intro/hover, raycast hitboxes, modal/social interactions and render loop. No filesystem enumeration, content hash, similarity index or duplicate grouping found in this entrypoint. Domain rejection strengthened; other111 original remaining blobs minus entrypoint still pending.",
    "LoadingManager explicitly supplied to GLTFLoader but texture/cube/audio loaders created independently, so manager onLoad does not prove all visible/audio assets ready. No-sound entry has click listener only and returns when global touchHappened true; regular entry has touchend listener. Social window.open result dereferenced without null check. These are source observations, no browser reproduction or fixes performed; unrelated UI issues not imported as duplicate-library requirements. No upstream code executed.",
    "Whole five SCSS files and two web manifests read. Styles implement theme maps, mobile breakpoints, typography, modals, loading screen and toggle controls; no duplicate-search logic. Theme lookup uses overlay-bg and scrollbar-track absent from both maps; source observation only, Sass/render outcome untested. Reset carries public-domain notice distinct from root MIT.",
    "Two manifests are byte-identical: same pinned Git blob and SHA256. Both declare root-absolute /web-app-manifest-{192,512}x{192,512}.png URLs while tracked icons reside in /media/{dark,light}-favicon/; no corresponding public-root files in pinned tree. This is static path mismatch, not HTTP/runtime test. Their equality is a concrete exact-duplicate asset pair; no image perceptual-equivalence claim.",
